&= 6x \cdot \left(a_{1}x^{1} + a_{2}x^{2} + a_{3}x^{3} + \cdots\right) - x^{2} \cdot \left(a_{0}x^{0} + a_{1}x^{1} + a_{2}x^{2} + \cdots \right) 
&= 6a_{1}x^{2} + 6x \cdot \left(a_{2}x^{2} + a_{3}x^{3} + \cdots \right) - x^{2}\cdot \left(a_{0}x^{0} + a_{1}x^{1}\right) -x^{2} \cdot \left(a_{2}x^{2} + a_{3}x^{3} + \cdots \right) 
&=  6a_{1}x^{2} + 6x \cdot A(x)  - x^{2}\cdot \left(a_{0}x^{0} + a_{1}x^{1}\right) -x^{2} \cdot A(x) 
A(x) \cdot \left(x^{2} - 6x + 1\right) &= 6a_{1}x^{2} -x^{2} \cdot \left(a_{0}x^{0} + a_{1}x^{1}\right) 
A(x) &= \frac{6a_{1}x^{2} -x^{2} \cdot \left(a_{0}x^{0} + a_{1}x^{1}\right)}{x^{2} - 6x + 1} 
&= \frac{x^{2} \cdot \left(6\cdot 22 - 4 \cdot 1 - 22 \cdot x^{1}\right)}{x^{2} - 6x + 1} 
&= \frac{x^{2} \cdot \left(128 - 22x\right)}{x^{2} - 6x + 1} 
\end{align*}

At this point we can use partial fractions.
We note that the roots of the denominator are: $x = \frac{6 \pm \sqrt{32}}{2} = 3 \pm 2\sqrt{2}$ We consider these  $r_{+}, r_{-} .$ So
\begin{align*}
\frac{128x^{2} - 22x^{3}}{(x - r_{+})(x - r_{-})} &= \frac{A}{x - r_{+}} + \frac{B}{x - r_{-}} 
128x^{2} - 22x^{3} &= A\cdot (x - r_{-}) + B\cdot (x - r_{+}) 
&= (A + B)x + \left(-Ar_{-} - Br_{+}\right)
\end{align*}
Hence  $A = -B$  and  $-Ar_{-} - Br_{+} = 0$  hence  $-\frac{A}{B}  = 1$  and  $-\frac{A}{B} = \frac{r_{+}}{r_{-}} .$</details>

