Let  $(i,j)$  denote the cell at the intersection of the  $i^{\text{th}}$  column and  $j^{\text{th}}$  row. At first we shall prove that there exists a sequence of  $n^2-1$  moves taking the pawn from  $(1,1)$  to  $(1,n)$  and visiting each cell exactly once. Let us carry out the proof by induction.

The base case  $n=1$  is trivial. The case  $n=2$  is solved by the following example:
[asy]
