For  $x=0$  we get  $f(0) = 2^rf(0)$  for all  $r$ , whence  $f(0) = 0$ ;
For  $x=1$  and  $t = 2^r > 0$  we get  $f(t) = t(a+\log_2 t)$  for arbitrary  $a$ , whence  $f(1) = a$ ;
For  $x=-1$  and  $t = 2^r > 0$  we get  $f(-t) = t(b-\log_2 t)$  for arbitrary  $b$ , whence  $f(-1) = b$ .

